      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-16T11:28:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The same write implementation is in the [cros_flash_it8xxx2.c](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/drivers/cros_flash/cros_flash_it8xxx2.c;l\u003d169-187;drc\u003d9263f14536b8ad64682362070d4f5fd7c1c8c7c6).\n\n\u003e There is EC_RES_BUSY\n\nHow would you use it to let EC handle other events? I think, this situation should be handled in the upper layers (e.g. host command handler) in the EC flash stack. It\u0027s not the driver\u0027s responsibility to think about other events in EC.\n\nOf course the same applies to `watchdog_reload()` used here, but for some reason, it\u0027s used in other drivers so I assumed this is standard practise.",
